  "prediction": "The report discusses the Senior Community Service Employment Program (SCSEP), which is a component of the Older Americans Act (OAA) that provides employment services to older adults with limited income. In FY2019, the SCSEP had a budget of $400 million and served over 60,000 participants. The program is administered by the Department of Labor (DOL) and is funded through the OAA. The report highlights the program's history, funding, and administration. In FY2018, 78% of the formula grant funds went to national grantees, while 22% went to state grantees. Grantees are required to meet performance targets set by the DOL, which include employment and earnings outcomes for participants. The report also mentions the demographic characteristics of SCSEP participants and their barriers to employment. The OAA also requires the DOL to report on program participation and performance.",
  "scored_prediction": "The report discusses the Senior Community Service Employment Program (SCSEP), which is a component of the Older Americans Act (OAA) that provides employment services to older adults with limited income. In FY2019, the SCSEP had a budget of $400 million and served over 60,000 participants. The program is administered by the Department of Labor (DOL) and is funded through the OAA. The report highlights the program's history, funding, and administration. In FY2018, 78% of the formula grant funds went to national grantees, while 22% went to state grantees. Grantees are required to meet performance targets set by the DOL, which include employment and earnings outcomes for participants. The report also mentions the demographic characteristics of SCSEP participants and their barriers to employment. The OAA also requires the DOL to report on program participation and performance.",
